5. PERSISTENCE
Two stores, no transaction. save() fire-and-forget writes localStorage["sched-v1"] (sync) and root.kv.schedule/"v1" (async, unawaited, no debounce — called on every keystroke from staff inputs). Concurrent in-flight kv writes can resolve out of order (last-resolution-wins, not last-call-wins).
Load precedence: kv first, else localStorage. Two sources of truth that can silently diverge (e.g. kv write fails but localStorage succeeds → next load resurrects the kv copy, discarding newer localStorage state).
Legacy migration (load()): pre-tkey schemas are downcast (Worker→Lead/Budtender, max*=8, everything non-Manager forced FT) with version stepping v2→v5. Current v5 forces all Managers manual and zeroes Manager needs.
Missing data: absent fields are backfilled (times/manual/events/opt guards + defaults()), so fresh boot is safe.
Malformed data: JSON.parse(raw) for localStorage sits outside any try/catch — corrupt localStorage throws, load() rejects, the boot .then() never runs, and the app renders nothing. kv path is guarded; localStorage path is not.
News cache: separate localStorage["planit-news-v2"] ({day, arts}), day-string expiry, stale-cache fallback. Survives independently of schedule data.
6. ARCHITECTURAL RISKS (identified, not solved)
One ~1,230-line file; ~90 globals sharing one mutable S — no ownership boundaries.
Scheduler, validator, scorer, and renderers all read/write the same live S.assign in place (buildSchedule resets it; pick pushes/pops trial assignments into it) — generation cannot run without clobbering live state; no pure/detached engine.
Business rules live inside render-adjacent code and DOM handlers (e.g. budget input handler, picker sort); rule text coupled by substring matching (§3.2).
save()+renderAll() invoked directly from ~25 UI sites — persistence coupled to keystrokes, no batching, no dirty-tracking.
Week navigation destroys S.assign (single-week memory) — real workforce history beyond fairHist aggregates is impossible.
Random ids (uid()) with no collision check; staff identity = opaque id, so fair-history continuity breaks silently on delete/re-add.
S.shifts fixed at six rows with no editor (needs are editable, rows are not) — the 49-slot structure is hardcoded by seed data, not by rule.
Dead code (renderDayGrid, renderPerson, counts() uses, S.opt.view) will mislead future refactors about supported views.
Test surface is one function (testLaborBudget, 5 asserts); the "8/8 validation scenarios" from project history exist only as tribal knowledge — not in the repo.
External CDN dependency at export time (cdnjs jsPDF) with no vendoring/fallback; news depends on live RSS via plugin proxy.
