8. MIGRATION PLAN (behavior-preserving, independently testable phases)
Phase 0 — Baseline lock (no refactor). Recover the 8 historical validation scenarios into tests/regression.js as data + expected violations; record current outputs (49-slot needs, 371 h demand, seed roster) as golden fixtures. Gate: all pass pre- and post-every phase.
Phase 1 — Pure-function extraction. Move time utils + shiftRange, paidHours/totalLabor, fatigue trio into modules with zero logic change; dual-run (old vs new, deep-compare) behind a flag. Gate: identical outputs on fixtures + live week.
Phase 2 — Violation codes. Give every validation message a stable code; scorer and rejection-hoist switch to codes, strings stay identical. Gate: scores and modals byte-identical.
Phase 3 — Store + persistence. Funnel mutations through store.js; add debounced single-writer persistence, malformed-data guard, kv/local divergence resolution. Gate: refresh/legacy-data upgrade tests; saved data format unchanged.
Phase 4 — Pure engine. buildSchedule operates on injected state, returns assignments; orchestrator commits. Fix the live-clobber pattern. Gate: 50-seed deterministic comparison old-vs-new generator.
Phase 5 — UI split. Move render/interaction files out one panel at a time; engine imports frozen. Gate: visual + interaction checklist per panel.
Phase 6 — xc unification. Resolve §3.1 with an explicit product decision (directional vs bidirectional) — deliberately last, as it's the only behavior-adjacent change.
